{
  "id": "m19l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Saneado y listas blancas",
    "en": "Sanitizing and allowlists"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Mejor permitir lo bueno que prohibir lo malo"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una **lista blanca** (allowlist) define lo que SÍ se acepta y rechaza todo lo demás. Es más segura que una lista negra, porque no tienes que adivinar todas las formas de ataque."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "permitidos = {'rojo', 'verde', 'azul'}",
          "def color_ok(c):",
          "    return c in permitidos",
          "",
          "print(color_ok('rojo'))",
          "print(color_ok(\"'; DROP TABLE--\"))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "True",
          "False"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Sanear** es quedarte solo con los caracteres permitidos. Por ejemplo, dejar únicamente letras y números."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def solo_alfanumerico(texto):",
          "    return ''.join(c for c in texto if c.isalnum())",
          "",
          "print(solo_alfanumerico('a1!b#2'))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "a1b2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Validar (¿es aceptable?) y sanear (límpialo) son complementarios; aplica ambos según el caso."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Better allow the good than ban the bad"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "An **allowlist** defines what IS accepted and rejects everything else. It's safer than a denylist because you don't have to guess every attack form."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "permitidos = {'rojo', 'verde', 'azul'}",
          "def color_ok(c):",
          "    return c in permitidos",
          "",
          "print(color_ok('rojo'))",
          "print(color_ok(\"'; DROP TABLE--\"))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "True",
          "False"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Sanitizing** is keeping only the allowed characters. For example, keeping only letters and numbers."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def solo_alfanumerico(texto):",
          "    return ''.join(c for c in texto if c.isalnum())",
          "",
          "print(solo_alfanumerico('a1!b#2'))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "a1b2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Validating (is it acceptable?) and sanitizing (clean it) are complementary; apply both as needed."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m19l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `solo_alfanumerico(texto)` que devuelva el texto con solo letras y números (quita el resto).",
        "en": "Define `solo_alfanumerico(texto)` returning the text with only letters and numbers (drop the rest)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def solo_alfanumerico(texto):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def solo_alfanumerico(texto):",
        "    return ''.join(c for c in texto if c.isalnum())"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Filtra con c.isalnum() dentro de un ''.join(...)."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Filter with c.isalnum() inside a ''.join(...)."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "solo_alfanumerico",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "a1!b#2"
              ],
              "expected": "a1b2"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "...---"
              ],
              "expected": ""
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "Hola Mundo"
              ],
              "expected": "HolaMundo"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m19l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `en_lista_blanca(valor, permitidos)` que devuelva True si `valor` está en la colección `permitidos`.",
        "en": "Define `en_lista_blanca(valor, permitidos)` returning True if `valor` is in the `permitidos` collection."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def en_lista_blanca(valor, permitidos):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def en_lista_blanca(valor, permitidos):",
        "    return valor in permitidos"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "El operador in comprueba pertenencia."
        ],
        "en": [
          "The in operator checks membership."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "en_lista_blanca",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "rojo",
                [
                  "rojo",
                  "azul"
                ]
              ],
              "expected": true
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "negro",
                [
                  "rojo",
                  "azul"
                ]
              ],
              "expected": false
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}